[1m[38;5;231mWhich structural approach should the spec use?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mA: Extract auth.mjs (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mlogin() moves to a DOM-free auth.mjs with injectable fetch; app.mjs does DOM wiring; node --test with a fake fetch.
[39m     [38;5;246mZero dependencies, src/ untouched. Requires renaming two files and one index.html edit.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m B: Stay in app.js, jsdom
     [38;5;246mNo file moves. Adds jsdom as the repo's first dependency, slower tests, and app.js keeps mixing network, [39m
     [38;5;246mvalidation, and DOM concerns.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m C: Dual CommonJS/global shim
     [38;5;246mauth.js works as both a browser global and a CommonJS module. Plain script tags and file:// keep working, but the [39m
     [38;5;246mshim is hand-rolled machinery that's easy to get subtly wrong.[39m
